 "public extract ^<Map[Symbol, Object]> = (\n			^extractMirror: mirror\n		)",
 "extractMirror: cdm <ClassDeclarationMirror> ^<Map[Symbol, Object]> = (\n			| result methods classMethods lazies nested |\n			result:: Map new.\n			result at: #name put: cdm name.\n			result at: #header put: cdm header source.\n			methods:: Map new.\n			cdm instanceSide methods do: [:m | methods at: m name put: m source ].\n			result at: #methods put: methods.\n			lazies:: Map new.\n			cdm instanceSide lazySlots do: [:ls | lazies at: ls name put: ls source ].\n			result at: #lazySlots put: lazies.\n			classMethods:: Map new.\n			cdm classSide methods do: [:m | classMethods at: m name put: m source ].\n			result at: #classMethods put: classMethods.\n			nested:: Map new.\n			cdm instanceSide nestedClasses do: [:nc |\n					nested at: nc name put: (extractMirror: nc)\n				].\n			result at: #nestedClasses put: nested.\n			^result\n		)",
 "public class ApplyStrategy new = Object new (\n		(* Abstract base for \"what happens when the user accepts a Changeset.\"\n   Concretes: RepoCommitStrategy for repository commits.\n   CommitVsParentStrategy for historical browsing (read-only).\n   Future: InstallToNamespaceStrategy for AI-proposal review,\n   StagedEditorsApplyStrategy for atomic install of unaccepted\n   editors. The dialog (ChangesetPresenter) renders the same way\n   regardless of strategy; the strategy supplies the action label,\n   message-field config, validation, the apply hook, and the\n   compute-changeset entry point. *)\n		\n	)",
