 "class VCSLib packageUsing: manifest = Object new (\n	(* MemoryHole — Pur version-control abstraction (Kleine et al., 2011),\n ported to the primordialsoup web runtime.\n\n Phase 1 of the port covers the abstraction core only:\n   - Core      (Repository / Historian / Version / Backend interfaces)\n   - Diffing   (text diff infrastructure; some Squeak-specific bits\n                are stubbed until we either port them or provide a\n                JS-backed differ)\n   - SourceMirrors (language-aware view of versioned source,\n                so commits and diffs are over Newspeak structure\n                rather than raw .ns text). Phase 4 of the web\n                port collapsed the Squeak-era Newspeak/Smalltalk\n                fork down to a single module — formerly\n                VCSNewspeakSourceMirrors, now just\n                VCSSourceMirrors.\n\n Deliberately NOT in this phase, to be added later in their own\n commits:\n   - UI            (VCSUI — needs Hopscotch-side rework anyway)\n   - Git backend   (the existing VCSGitBackendProvider shells out\n                    via ExternalLauncher; the web replacement will be\n                    a new VCSIsomorphicGitBackendProvider backed by\n                    isomorphic-git + lightning-fs IndexedDB storage)\n   - hg / svn      (no path to the browser; archived)\n   - SmalltalkSourceMirrors  (Squeak-only; archived)\n   - VCSImageMirrorCaching   (Squeak-specific perf cache; revisit\n                              if needed once a backend exists) *)\n	\n	|\n		Core = manifest VCSCore.\n		Diffing = manifest VCSDiffing.\n		SourceMirrors = manifest VCSSourceMirrors.\n	|\n)",
 "new",
 "new",
 "public usingPlatform: p ide: ide = (\n		^VCS usingPlatform: p ide: ide\n	)",
 "class VCS usingPlatform: p ide: ide = Object new (\n		(* The original Squeak MemoryHole used `|| ... ||` simultaneous slots\n so the four sub-module initializers could mutually reference each\n other (each module's slot block reads vcs.<sibling>). In\n primordialsoup the `||` machinery wants a Future class in scope\n that this module doesn't expose, and the resulting submodule\n instantiation fails with `MessageNotUnderstood: VCS Future`.\n\n Web-port pattern: store the factory args, expose each sub-module\n as a `lazy public` slot. Sub-modules are then constructed on first\n access. The cycle the `||` was solving is broken in parallel by\n deferring each sub-module's cross-module dependencies to its own\n lazy slots (see VCSCore / VCSSourceMirrors). End-to-end behaviour\n is the same as before: by the time\n user code calls a method that needs a sibling module, every\n module's slot block has run. *)\n		\n		|\n			private platformHolder = p.\n			private ideHolder = ide.\n		|\n	)",
 "new",
 "new",
 "lazy public core = Core usingPlatform: platformHolder vcs: self ide: ideHolder.",
