 "class V5BytecodeSimulation usingPlatform: platform = (\n	(* V5 bytecode interpretation for the JS platform's debugger and tooling, ported from github.com/rmacnak/primordialsoup newspeak/Mirrors.ns at commit 338f0bb342a618f5608ab72ab1b1fae9b226e472 (extract preserved as upstream-V5Simulator-338f0bb3.ns.txt).\n\nInstructionStream is the stateless decoder: interpretNextInstruction fetches the instruction at the current bci, advances the bci, and dispatches to one operation method per instruction kind. Subclasses supply the machine: the Disassembler here renders instruction strings (tests, senders/implementors, debugger display); the Simulator (execution over the NS2JS runtime's MM bytecode records) is the next port step and will be a sibling subclass.\n\nThe subclass protocol InstructionStream requires: method (understanding bytecode and literals, both one-origin indexable), bci, bci:, and the operation methods — push:, pushReceiver, pushMixin, pushParameter:, pushLocal:, popIntoLocal:, storeIntoLocal:, pushIndirectLocal:inVector:, popIntoIndirectLocal:inVector:, storeIntoIndirectLocal:inVector:, pop, dup, jump:, popJumpTrue:, popJumpFalse:, ordinarySend:numArgs:, selfSend:numArgs:, implicitReceiverSend:numArgs:, superSend:numArgs:, eventualSend:numArgs:, outerSend:numArgs:depth:, pushNewArray:, pushNewArrayWithElements:, pushEnclosingObject:, pushClosureNumCopied:numArgs:blockSize:, returnLocal:, returnLocalReceiver, returnLocalTop, returnNonLocal:, returnNonLocalReceiver, returnNonLocalTop, unusedBytecode.\n\nDeviation from upstream, deliberate: upstream's one-byte dispatch decodes bytes 48-63 as popJumpTrue:, but the emitter assigns that range to the short forms of popJumpFalse: (a confirmed upstream Simulator bug, see BYTECODES_V5_SPEC_2026-07-13.md section 6); fixed here. Our own emitter only produces the three-byte branch forms, so the short forms matter only for foreign bytecode. *)\n\n	|\n		private List = platform collections List.\n	|\n)",
