 "public top ^<Object> = (\n			stackPointer < 1 ifTrue: [\n					Error signal: 'Simulated operand stack underflow ' , describe\n				].\n			^frame at: stackPointer\n		)",
 "public class SimulatedMethod record: r mixin: m selector: s accessModifier: am = Object new (\n		(* An MM bytecode record paired with its owning runtime mixin (records do not carry their mixin; it is captured at lookup time) under the decoder's method protocol: bytecode, literals. The record layout is [bytes, literals, numArgs, numLocals, maxStack, bciMap, sourceStart], per Newspeak2JSCompilation encodeBytecodeOf:. The record is nil for JS-only methods: activation of such a method is the full-speed escape. *)\n\n		|\n			public record = r.\n			public mixin = m.\n			public selector <Symbol> = s.\n			public accessModifier <Symbol> = am.\n\n			(* The MM metadata entry itself, for the source index. *)\n			public metadata\n\n			(* Direct source text for methods with no MM entry (runtime-compiled doIts). *)\n			public sourceText\n\n			(* The V5 DebugInfo computed when this method was compiled at runtime (doIts): local names and bci mappings without recompilation, psoup-style (psoup stores DebugInfo as the doIt method's metadata). *)\n			public debugInfo\n		|\n	)",
